al":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 2be2cbb720e4b2c2fa11e677c73d4371c4ab47b9 onwards\n- Not reproducible in Godot 4.4.1\n\n### System information\n\nAny\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen I wrote https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107782, I forgot that HDR 2D still uses a 10-bit viewport buffer on the Mobile Rendering method, so this means that viewport-based debanding must still be active with HDR 2D enabled, but it should be 10-bit aligned dithering rather than 8-bit aligned dithering.\n\nEnd result is that non-material based effects like Glow effects no longer have functioning debanding:\n\n| 4.4.1 | masater\n| --- | ---\n| <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fd7947ff-c93f-496f-b5c1-4d2b99bb4c8b\" /> | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a6667e9d-5140-4606-919b-a93a574f2b8c\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a project with Mobile rendering method\n- Enable HDR 2D\n- Set up a scene that uses environment effects like Glow\n- Enable debanding\n- Note that it doesn't work on the environment effects\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mobile-debanding.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21322782/mobile-debanding.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url"